hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","Book of Purification. Al-Lu'lu'i said: Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Sulayman ibn Abi al-Sa'ib informed us, from Talhah ibn Abi Qanan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wanted to urinate, would go to rough, uneven ground, take a stick, poke the soil with it until it was loosened, then urinate."
"2","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from al-Hasan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered the privy, would say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil and evildoing, filthy, impure, accursed Satan."
"3","Hisham ibn Khalid narrated to us, al-Walid informed us, from Ibn Jabir, from Makhul, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade urinating at the doors of the mosque."
"4","Amr ibn Awn narrated to us, Waki' informed us, from Zam'ah ibn Salih, from Isa ibn Azdad, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you urinates, let him shake his private part three times."
"5","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah ibn Sufyan narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, from Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Qurashi, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you drink, sip your drink, and when you use the tooth-stick, use it across the teeth."
